  "prefLabel": "En 1012.13 Group Study Results Meeting",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1012.13 Group Study Results Meeting. The utility shall conduct a meeting to discuss the group study results with the applicant and all other applicants with facilities in the common study area within 20 business days of providing the group study results to the applicant. The group study results meeting shall:\n\n(a) Take place in person, by telephone, or virtually;\n\n(b) The utility and the applicant shall bring to the meeting personnel, including system engineers, and other resources as might be reasonably required to accomplish the purpose of the meeting; and\n\n(c) By mutual agreement of the parties, the group study results meeting may be waived.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
